  "_note": "v7 = v6 with the preference legs REBUILT as SHORT COMPLETE TURNS and with the train/eval format mismatch fixed in evals.py. (1) Preference legs now FILTER for pairs whose responses are naturally <=96 tokens and prompts <=256 \u2014 no mid-sentence truncation, no tail-capped prompts. Discard is brutal by design (HelpSteer2 keeps 127 of 10162 pairs; its responses are inherently long) \u2014 a truncated turn ends mid-sentence and is not something the model ever saw. (2) evals.py now tokenises eval prompts as f'{prompt}\\n', matching data.py format_row, so the model is scored on the prefix shape it was TRAINED on. That changes EVERY leg's absolute numbers, so v7 results are NOT comparable to v6/earlier \u2014 this is a fresh baseline by design. (3) evaluate_mcq now reports discarded_examples and warns above 2%; the prompt cap is derived from max_length instead of guessed. hs2_cor_val dropped (62 rows, 6.4pt floor). | v8 = v7 + two CODE preference legs. `themis_py` (project-themis/Themis-CodePreference, language=1 Python, aspect=3 FUNCTIONAL CORRECTNESS; 71031 pairs -> 8701 short-turn -> 1200) is the best-shaped preference leg built so far: leak 2%, gold 198 vs distractor 200 chars (-3), shortest-picker excess +1.1 pts, and pair similarity median 0.974 with 87% above 0.8 \u2014 chosen and rejected are the SAME program with a bug fixed, an objective minimal pair. NEVER truncate this source: the first differing token is at median 40 but p90 190, so cutting to 96 tokens makes 24% of pairs BYTE-IDENTICAL; use short-turn FILTERING only (the builder now also guards with a `degenerate` counter). `python_dpo` (NextWealth/Python-DPO, chosen_code vs rejected_code-1, 153 rows) is included ON REQUEST but FAILS GATE 1: gold 454 vs distractor 188 chars (+266) and a shortest-picker excess of -41.8 pts, i.e. 'pick the longest' wins ~92%; pair similarity 0.179 so they are not minimal pairs at all. KEEP IT OUT OF COMPOSITES \u2014 it is a verbosity axis.",
