    "hs2_short": "SNR 0.53 and rho(alone, full battery) = -0.008; only 127 pairs survive the short-turn filter, so it cannot be rebuilt bigger",
    "openbookqa": "r=0.88 with commonsenseqa; pure duplication at high SNR"
  },
  "notes": "v10 = v9 with per-leg item caps sized from measured data. For each leg the smallest item count whose ARM RANKING still matches the full leg at Spearman >= 0.95 was measured on the 42-arm warm set (reasoning_core.reports.leg_sizing), then multiplied by 1.5 as a safety margin and floored at 100. Dev legs (bbh_dev_nomenu, uf_short, python_dpo) are never shrunk. No leg is removed relative to v9 -- this cuts item COUNT only, so every leg present in v9 is still reported.",
